# Build context exclusions for `langgraph build` (see scripts/build_image.sh).
#
# The Dockerfile that `langgraph build` generates does `ADD . /deps/langgraph`, so
# anything left here lands in an image layer and is readable by anyone who can pull
# the image. Without this file the image shipped `.env` — Azure keys, the LangSmith
# key, and CORDIA_TENANT_CONTEXT_SIGNING_KEYS, which is the JWS key the agent
# authenticates to the .NET API with — plus a 300 MB `.venv`.
#
# Secrets belong in the runtime environment, never in the image.

# Local credentials. `.env` is gitignored, so CI never had it — but anyone building
# from a working tree does, and `bun nx run langgraph:docker-build` is documented.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The virtualenv is rebuilt inside the image. Leaving it in is both the bulk of the
# build context and a way to ship host-platform binaries into a Linux image.
.venv

# `langgraph dev` scratch state (checkpoint store pickles).
.langgraph_api/

# Python build/test detritus. These need `**/` — .dockerignore matches with Go's
# filepath.Match, so a bare `__pycache__/` matches only at the context root and
# leaves every nested one behind. Verified: without the `**/`, the built image
# still carried cordia_agent/**/__pycache__/*.pyc.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# Not needed at runtime.
tests/
.git/
.gitignore
